  "description": "Natural oil seeps at ~1180 m depth (Mega Plume vent). Oil rises from the seafloor continuously; a slick appears on the surface near the vent at ~2–7 m/s wind and lives for a few hours. There are other Green Canyon seeps in the area, so slicks far from the vent are not necessarily errors. NISAR L-band images, VV 5 MHz (coarser resolution); the 'oil-likeness' score is a ranking for review, not proof. The seep is always active, so 'before' is an image of the same track with no slick at the vent (it can be later than other dates).",
  "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7387546",
